==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|seewey|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|sǣweġ||a sea-way, a path through the sea}}, equivalent to {{compound|sea|way|lang=en}}. Compare {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Seegang||seaway|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːweɪ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} a [[lane]] or [[route]] at [[sea]] that is [[regularly]] used by [[ship]]s; a [[sea lane]] or [[trade route]]
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} an [[inland]] [[waterway]] used by [[seagoing]] [[shipping]]
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} the [[headway]] of a [[vessel]]

